Z||000000||cadaver||06-05-2001||10:54 PM||||I was driving up to bakersfield. That about 160 miles north from LA. Guage never moved up a tick. I stopped to get something to drink and noticed a drip from near the water pump. Well I just left it and would fix it when I got home the next day. I open the cap and poured in 1 liter of water and used the pressure tester.(the best investment for working on a cooling system) Pumped it up to 20 psi. I know the stock system is only 16psi. But if it leaks at 20 then it will leak at 16 soon enough. Well at 20 I found 5 leaks. The hose as it attaches to the timing cover. The left hand hose at the pipe. The left pipe plug and both ends of the hose from the pump to the trunk wall. That hose was leaking through the skin. It is really old. Replaced it for $8 and now its leak free again. Just basically babbling.||||reg||1
